us 2 but as X gets  larger and larger meaning as you go to  the right on the graph this quantity  here is going to get smaller and smaller  it's going to approach 0 so we just end  up with the quotient here you don't have  to worry about the remainder because  that term is going to go to 0 so but for  number 2 here we're gonna do the long  division so x squared goes into X cubed  how many times that's one time I  distribute the X I get X you  plus four X I subtract okay so these are  going to cancel this gives us 3x squared  plus twelve and then how many times does  x squared go into X up to 3x squared  that's three times so my distribute I  get 3x squared plus twelve I subtract  you can see there's a zero remainder but  you don't have to worry about the  remainder just the quotient here so y  equals x plus three is going to be our  slant asymptote for this rational  function if you want to see more about  graphing rational functions check out  the video right there and I'll see over  in that video if you're joining my my  videos subscribe to the channel my goal  for you is to make learning math less  stressful so you can raise your grade  pass your class and go on to pursue your  dreams I'll see you in my future videos
 

